Pizza Legacy v@PLEGACY_VERSION_FULL@ - macOS Release (Apple Silicon)
====================================================

@README_INTRO@

FIRST LAUNCH – macOS security message
--------------------------------------

On recent versions of macOS, you may see a message saying:

    "Pizza Legacy" is damaged and can't be opened.
     You should move it to the Bin.

This is a macOS security restriction (Gatekeeper) that appears because
the app is not signed with an Apple Developer certificate.

The app is not actually damaged.

To allow it to run, open Terminal and run:

    xattr -cr "/path/to/Pizza Legacy.app"

Tip: You can type `xattr -cr ` (with a space), then drag the app into
Terminal to fill in the path automatically.

Then try opening the app again.

You only need to do this once.

Alternative method (if available):

After attempting to open the app once, go to:
System Settings -> Privacy & Security

If an "Open Anyway" option appears (near the bottom), you can use that instead.


